# Chalk in vinegar: why this is not a rubbery-bone model
# Acid removes carbonate from chalk. Real bone is a composite: calcium-phosphate
# mineral reinforces collagen. Acid can leave that collagen scaffold flexible;
# chalk contains no collagen, so dissolving it cannot predict bone bending.
register lv1
add v1 water 50mL
add v1 chalk_stick 2g
look v1
new beaker
add v2 white_vinegar_5_percent 50mL
add v2 chalk_stick 2g
look v2
inspect v1
inspect v2

# The matched control honestly computes acid–carbonate dissolution and carbon
# dioxide. It is evidence about chalk only. No bone species, collagen scaffold,
# mechanical stiffness or bending observable exists in this model.
